 to run  things like your refrigerator your lamps  your Wi-Fi router and of course charge  up your cell phones but taking it even  further it can run a CPAP machine for up  to 15 hours which means it could  literally be a life saver not only that  but the most impressive thing is that it  works as a UPS no not the delivery  service UPS stands for uninterruptible  power source so if your power goes out  this power station will automatically  kick on and Supply Power without your  machine or device that's connected to it  shutting down at all now we actually  used UPS machines in our office in the  case of a power outage so that if the  power goes out our computers and our  data server will continue to run without  instantly shutting down which is  extremely important because our data  could get corrupted and we can lose  files if it wasn't for having them  connected to UPS machines so the fact  that this power station doubles as a UPS  is incredible because you can just leave  it at home plugged into the wall and  have your computers and whatever else  plugged into it just in case the power  goes out and then when you actually need  to take it somewhere on the go on some  kind of trip or whatever else it'll be  fully charged up and ready to go now  moving further let's talk about some of  the other features first off it comes  with two convenient handles that make it  very nice to carry around with it being  36 pounds which is actually very compact  if you consider just how much battery  power is packed into this thing  especially since it doesn't come with an  external power brick everything is built  in now on top of that as you can see it  also has a built-in display which  basically tells you the battery life  percentage left the total output power  that you're using to charge your devices  the time remaining if the output power  remains consistent at the current levels  which is very convenient and you also  get the total input power if you're  charging it and a